The debrief demonstrates significantly higher emotional intelligence than the roleplay itself. The respondent shows sophisticated understanding of relational ethics, subtext, and what they *should* have done—yet this insight doesn't fully translate into the roleplay performance. This suggests either performance anxiety, role-playing constraints, or a gap between intellectual understanding and real-time application.
